Troubleshooting Tips
Common Issues and Solutions
Issue 1: Snapshot Creation Fails

Symptom: Snapshot remains in "InProgress" state
Solution: Check storage class supports snapshots and has sufficient space
# Check storage class capabilities
oc get storageclass -o yaml

# Check PVC status
oc get pvc -n default
Issue 2: VM Restore Fails

Symptom: Restore operation fails or VM won't start
Solution: Ensure VM is stopped before restoration
# Force stop VM if needed
oc patch vm test-vm --type merge -p '{"spec":{"running":false}}' -n default

# Check VM status
oc get vm test-vm -n default -o yaml
Issue 3: CronJob Not Executing

Symptom: No automated snapshots created
Solution: Check RBAC permissions and CronJob configuration
# Check CronJob status
oc describe cronjob vm-snapshot-automation -n default

# Check service account permissions
oc auth can-i create vmsnapshot --as=system:serviceaccount:default:snapshot-automation-sa
Issue 4: Too Many Snapshots

Symptom: Storage space running low
Solution: Implement cleanup policies
# Manual cleanup of old snapshots
oc get vmsnapshot -n default --sort-by=.metadata.creationTimestamp

# Delete specific snapshot
oc delete vmsnapshot SNAPSHOT_NAME -n default
Best Practices
Snapshot Naming Convention: Use consistent naming with timestamps
Retention Policy: Implement automatic cleanup of old snapshots
Monitoring: Set up alerts for snapshot failures
Testing: Regularly test restore procedures
Documentation: Maintain records of snapshot schedules and retention policies
